  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Bhudeo vs State Of U.P. on 18 November, 2019 Author: Sunita Agarwal Bench: Sunita Agarwal High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 41 Case :- Criminal Revision No. - 1200 of 1999 Revisionist :- Bhudeo",
    "facts": "The allegations against the revisionist are of adulteration of milk based on the report of the Public Analyst wherein it is noted that the fat content in the sample of cow milk was found less than the standard. As per the standard, fat content in the milk ought to be 3.5, whereas it was found 2.9 in the milk sample collected on 31.03.1988. The revisionist was nabbed by the Food Inspector while he was going on cycle with the container to sell the milk.",
    "arguments": "The submission of learned counsel for the revisionist is that the sample collected from the revisionist was not found adulterated with any hazardous substance and further on account of delay caused in getting the Public Analyst report, opportunity of the revisionist under Section 13 (2) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act' 1954 has been taken away. Bhudeo vs State Of U.P. on 18 November, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/152140553/ 1 The Apex Court in the case of Vijendra vs. State of UP reported in AIR 2019 SC 4351 has held that the requirement of Section 13(2) of the Food and Adulteration Act to send the report after institution of prosecution against the person within time prescribed under Rule 9B of Rules, 1955 is mandatory and substantial compliance of the said provision is needed to sustain the conviction.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The submission of learned counsel for the revisionist is that the sample collected from the revisionist was not found adulterated with any hazardous substance and further on account of delay caused in getting the Public Analyst report, opportunity of the revisionist under Section 13 (2) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act' 1954 has been taken away. Bhudeo vs State Of U.P. on 18 November, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/152140553/ 1",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "The Apex Court in the case of Vijendra vs. State of UP reported in AIR 2019 SC 4351 has held that the requirement of Section 13(2) of the Food and Adulteration Act to send the report after institution of prosecution against the person within time prescribed under Rule 9B of Rules, 1955 is mandatory and substantial compliance of the said provision is needed to sustain the conviction."
  },
